{title: 419 - Soon Shall the Trump of God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #419 • UNITED MAN • 6.6.9.6}
{lyricist: Anon}
{composer: Norman L. Warren}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 419}
{meta: tune UNITED MAN}
{meta: meter 6.6.9.6}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Soon [Ab/Eb]shall [Eb]the [Ab/Eb]trump [Eb]of [Ab]God
[Gm]Give [Cm]out the welcome [Gm]sound,
[G7/F]That shakes [Bb/D]death's [Cm]silent [Bb]chamber [Cm]walls,
[B]And [Eb/Bb]breaks [Gm]the [Ab]turf [Bb7]sealed [Eb]ground.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]You [Ab/Eb]dwellers in [Eb]the [Ab]dust,
[Gm]Awake, [Cm]come forth, and [Gm]sing;
[G7/F]Sharp [Eb]has [Bb/D]your [Cm]frost [Ab/C]of [Bb]winter [Cm]been,
[B]But [Eb/Bb]bright [Gm]shall [Ab]be [Bb7]your [Eb]spring.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]'Twas [Ab/Eb]sown [Eb]in [Ab/Eb]weakness here;
[Gm]'Twill then [Cm]be raised in power;
[G7/F]That [Eb]which [Bb/D]was [Cm]sown [Ab/C]in [Bb]earthly [Cm]seed
[B]Shall rise [Eb/Bb]a [Gm]heav'nly [Bb7]flower.
{end_of_verse}
